      *
      *The reserved words in use: small snippets grouped by division, so
      *each word appears in the clause or statement the reference gives
      *it to, rather than in a bare list. Words with no snippet yet are
      *gathered at the end, so the whole of Appendix E stays covered.
      *
      *Member: CBLWORDS  Compilable: no (snippets, not a whole program)
      *Source: ILE COBOL Language Reference SC09-2539.
      *Retrieved: 2026-07-29
      *
      *The Identification Division and its paragraphs.
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. CBLWORDS IS INITIAL PROGRAM.
       AUTHOR. EXAMPLE LTD.
       INSTALLATION. HEAD OFFICE.
       DATE-WRITTEN. 2026-07-29.
       DATE-COMPILED.
       SECURITY. NONE.
      *
      *The Environment Division: the computer paragraphs, the
      *special names, and a file-control entry of each organization.
       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       CONFIGURATION SECTION.
       SOURCE-COMPUTER. IBM-ISERIES WITH DEBUGGING MODE.
       OBJECT-COMPUTER. IBM-ISERIES
             MEMORY SIZE 32768 WORDS
             SEGMENT-LIMIT IS 20
             PROGRAM COLLATING SEQUENCE IS NATIVE.
       SPECIAL-NAMES.
           ALPHABET STD-1 IS STANDARD-1
           ALPHABET STD-2 IS STANDARD-2
           ALPHABET EBC IS EBCDIC
           CLASS HEXCHAR IS "0" THRU "9" "A" THRU "F"
           CONSOLE IS TYPEWRITER
           SYSTEM-CONSOLE IS SYSCON
           REQUESTOR IS WORKSTATION
           LOCAL-DATA IS LDA
           ATTRIBUTE-DATA IS ATTRDATA
           SYSTEM-SHUTDOWN IS SHUTDOWN-SW
           OPEN-FEEDBACK IS OPNFB
           I-O-FEEDBACK IS IOFB
           CURRENCY SIGN IS "$"
           DECIMAL-POINT IS COMMA
           LINKAGE TYPE IS PROGRAM FOR "NEXTPGM".
       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
       FILE-CONTROL.
           SELECT OPTIONAL ARCH-FILE ASSIGN TO DISK-ARCHIVE
             ORGANIZATION IS SEQUENTIAL ACCESS MODE IS SEQUENTIAL
             RESERVE 2 AREAS FILE STATUS IS WS-STATUS.
           SELECT ORDER-FILE ASSIGN TO DATABASE-ORDHDR
             ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
             RECORD KEY IS ORD-KEY WITH DUPLICATES.
           SELECT REL-FILE ASSIGN TO DISK-RELWORK
             ORGANIZATION IS RELATIVE ACCESS MODE IS RANDOM
             RELATIVE KEY IS WS-RRN.
           SELECT SORT-WORK ASSIGN TO DISK-SORTWK.
           SELECT IDX2-FILE ASSIGN TO DATABASE-ORDIDX
             ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
             RECORD KEY IS ORD-KEY
             ALTERNATE RECORD KEY IS ORD-DATA WITH DUPLICATES.
           SELECT TAPE-FILE ASSIGN TO TAPEFILE-QTAPE.
           SELECT DKT-FILE ASSIGN TO DISKETTE-QDKT.
           SELECT FMT-FILE ASSIGN TO FORMATFILE-ORDFMT-SI.
           SELECT NUL-FILE ASSIGN TO DATABASE-ORDNUL-ALWNULL.
           SELECT DSP-FILE ASSIGN TO WORKSTATION-ORDDSP-SI
             ORGANIZATION IS TRANSACTION
             CONTROL-AREA IS WS-CTLAREA.
       I-O-CONTROL.
           RERUN ON ARCH-FILE EVERY 100 RECORDS OF ORDER-FILE
           SAME RECORD AREA FOR ARCH-FILE ORDER-FILE
           SAME SORT-MERGE AREA FOR SORT-WORK
           MULTIPLE FILE TAPE CONTAINS TAPE-FILE POSITION 1
           COMMITMENT CONTROL FOR ORDER-FILE.
      *
      *The Data Division: a file description carrying its clauses, a
      *sort description, and working storage using every usage and
      *the data description clauses.
       DATA DIVISION.
       FILE SECTION.
       FD  ORDER-FILE
             BLOCK CONTAINS 10 RECORDS
             RECORD CONTAINS 80 CHARACTERS
             LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD
             DATA RECORDS ARE ORDER-RECORD
             LINAGE IS 60 LINES WITH FOOTING AT 55
             LINES AT TOP 3 LINES AT BOTTOM 2
             CODE-SET IS EBC.
       01  ORDER-RECORD.
               05  ORD-KEY               PIC X(10).
               05  ORD-DATA              PIC X(70).
       FD  DSP-FILE.
       01  DSP-REC                   PIC X(80).
       SD  SORT-WORK.
       01  SORT-RECORD               PIC X(80).
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       77  WS-STATUS                 PIC XX.
       77  WS-RRN                    PIC 9(9) USAGE BINARY.
       77  WS-CTLAREA                PIC X(12).
       77  WS-DATE                   FORMAT DATE "@Y-%m-%d".
       77  WS-EDIT                   PICTURE IS $$,$$9.99CR.
       01  ORDER-T TYPEDEF.
               05  OT-NBR                PIC 9(7).
       77  WS-ORDER                  TYPE ORDER-T.
       77  WS-TWIN                   LIKE WS-CTLAREA.
       01  WS-STATUS-FLAGS.
               05  WS-STAT               PIC XX.
                   88  GOOD-STATUS       VALUES ARE "00" "97".
               05  FILLER                PIC X(5) VALUE ALL "*".
               05  WS-JUST               PIC X(6) JUST.
               05  WS-SYNC               PIC S9(4) BINARY SYNC.
               05  WS-COMP               PIC S9(4) COMP.
               05  WS-DBCS               PIC G(3) USAGE DISPLAY-1.
       01  WS-USAGES IS GLOBAL.
               05  U-COMP                PIC S9(4) USAGE COMPUTATIONAL.
               05  U-COMP-1              USAGE COMP-1.
               05  U-COMP-2              USAGE COMP-2.
               05  U-COMP-3              PIC S9(7)V99 USAGE COMP-3.
               05  U-COMP-4              PIC S9(9) USAGE COMP-4.
               05  U-PACKED              PIC S9(5) PACKED-DECIMAL.
               05  U-DISPLAY             PIC ZZ9.99- USAGE DISPLAY.
               05  U-NATL                PIC N(4) USAGE NATIONAL.
               05  U-INDEX               USAGE INDEX.
               05  U-POINTER             USAGE POINTER.
               05  U-PROCPTR             USAGE PROCEDURE-POINTER.
               05  U-COMP5               PIC S9(9) USAGE COMP-5.
               05  U-CN1                 USAGE COMPUTATIONAL-1.
               05  U-CN2                 USAGE COMPUTATIONAL-2.
               05  U-CN3                 PIC S9(5) COMPUTATIONAL-3.
               05  U-CN4                 PIC S9(5) COMPUTATIONAL-4.
               05  U-CN5                 PIC S9(5) COMPUTATIONAL-5.
       01  WS-TABLE-AREA IS EXTERNAL.
               05  WS-ROW OCCURS 1 TO 12 TIMES
                   DEPENDING ON WS-RRN
                   ASCENDING KEY IS WS-COL
                   INDEXED BY WS-IX.
                   10  WS-COL            PIC X(4).
       01  WS-REDEF.
               05  WS-AMOUNT             PIC S9(7)V99 SIGN IS TRAILING
                   SEPARATE CHARACTER.
               05  WS-LEAD               PIC S9(5) SIGN LEADING.
               05  WS-ZERO-FILL          PIC 9(5) BLANK WHEN ZERO.
               05  WS-RIGHT              PIC X(8) JUSTIFIED RIGHT.
               05  WS-SYNCED             PIC S9(4) BINARY SYNCHRONIZED.
       01  WS-OVER REDEFINES WS-REDEF   PIC X(30).
       66  WS-PART RENAMES WS-AMOUNT THRU WS-LEAD.
       LOCAL-STORAGE SECTION.
       77  LS-WORK                   PIC 9(5) VALUE ZERO.
       LINKAGE SECTION.
       01  LK-PARM                   PIC X(10).
      *
      *The Procedure Division: declaratives, then each statement in
      *a small snippet of its own.
       PROCEDURE DIVISION USING BY REFERENCE LK-PARM.
       DECLARATIVES.
       IO-ERR SECTION.
           USE AFTER STANDARD EXCEPTION PROCEDURE ON ORDER-FILE.
       IO-ERR-PARA.
           CONTINUE.
       END DECLARATIVES.
       MAIN SECTION 50.
       FILE-VERBS.
           OPEN INPUT ORDER-FILE OUTPUT ARCH-FILE I-O REL-FILE
           OPEN EXTEND ARCH-FILE
           OPEN INPUT ARCH-FILE REVERSED
           READ ORDER-FILE NEXT RECORD WITH NO LOCK
             AT END CONTINUE NOT AT END CONTINUE END-READ
           READ ORDER-FILE FIRST RECORD END-READ
           READ ORDER-FILE LAST RECORD END-READ
           READ ORDER-FILE PRIOR RECORD END-READ
           READ ORDER-FILE KEY IS ORD-KEY
             INVALID KEY CONTINUE NOT INVALID KEY CONTINUE END-READ
           START ORDER-FILE KEY IS GREATER THAN ORD-KEY END-START
           WRITE ORDER-RECORD FROM WS-REDEF
             BEFORE ADVANCING 2 LINES END-WRITE
           WRITE ORDER-RECORD AFTER ADVANCING PAGE END-WRITE
           WRITE ORDER-RECORD AT END-OF-PAGE CONTINUE
             NOT AT EOP CONTINUE END-WRITE
           IF LINAGE-COUNTER GREATER THAN 55 CONTINUE END-IF
           WRITE SUBFILE DSP-REC FORMAT IS "SFL01" END-WRITE
           REWRITE ORDER-RECORD INVALID KEY CONTINUE END-REWRITE
           DELETE ORDER-FILE END-DELETE
           UNLOCK ORDER-FILE
           CLOSE ORDER-FILE WITH LOCK REEL FOR REMOVAL
           CLOSE ARCH-FILE UNIT WITH NO REWIND
           COMMIT
           ROLLBACK.
       SCREEN-VERBS.
           ACQUIRE WS-CTLAREA FOR DSP-FILE
           ACCEPT WS-CTLAREA FROM CONSOLE
           ACCEPT WS-RRN FROM DAY-OF-WEEK
           ACCEPT WS-RRN FROM DAY
           ACCEPT WS-RRN FROM TIME
           ACCEPT WS-CTLAREA WITH NO-ECHO
           DISPLAY WS-CTLAREA UPON CRT WITH NO ADVANCING
           DROP WS-CTLAREA FROM DSP-FILE
           SET U-POINTER TO ADDRESS OF WS-REDEF.
      *The extended ACCEPT and DISPLAY of the workstation, whose
      *phrases name the display attributes.
       EXTENDED-DISPLAY.
           DISPLAY WS-CTLAREA AT LINE 5 COLUMN 10 WITH BELL BLINK
             HIGHLIGHT REVERSE-VIDEO UNDERLINE BLANK SCREEN
             FOREGROUND-COLOR 7 BACKGROUND-COLOR 1
           ACCEPT WS-CTLAREA AT LINE 5 COL 30 WITH AUTO-SKIP BEEP
             FULL REQUIRED SECURE UPDATE PROMPT RIGHT-JUSTIFY
             TRAILING-SIGN END-ACCEPT.
       ARITHMETIC-VERBS.
           ADD 1 TO WS-RRN ROUNDED
             ON SIZE ERROR CONTINUE NOT ON SIZE ERROR CONTINUE END-ADD
           ADD WS-RRN TO WS-RRN GIVING WS-RRN END-ADD
           ADD CORRESPONDING WS-REDEF TO WS-REDEF END-ADD
           SUBTRACT 1 FROM WS-RRN END-SUBTRACT
           SUBTRACT CORR WS-REDEF FROM WS-REDEF END-SUBTRACT
           MULTIPLY 2 BY WS-RRN END-MULTIPLY
           DIVIDE 2 INTO WS-RRN GIVING WS-RRN
             REMAINDER WS-AMOUNT END-DIVIDE
           COMPUTE WS-RRN = WS-RRN ** 2 END-COMPUTE
           INITIALIZE WS-REDEF REPLACING NUMERIC DATA BY ZERO.
       FLOW-VERBS.
           IF WS-STATUS IS EQUAL TO "00" OR LESS THAN "10" AND
              NOT GREATER THAN OR EQUAL TO "90"
             CONTINUE
           ELSE
             CONTINUE
           END-IF
           IF WS-CTLAREA IS ALPHABETIC-UPPER CONTINUE END-IF
           IF WS-CTLAREA IS NOT ALPHABETIC-LOWER CONTINUE END-IF
           IF WS-RRN IS POSITIVE CONTINUE END-IF
           IF WS-AMOUNT IS NEGATIVE CONTINUE END-IF
           EVALUATE TRUE ALSO FALSE
             WHEN "A" THRU "M" ALSO ANY CONTINUE
             WHEN OTHER CONTINUE
           END-EVALUATE
           PERFORM FILE-VERBS THROUGH SCREEN-VERBS
             WITH TEST AFTER VARYING WS-RRN FROM 1 BY 1
             UNTIL WS-RRN > 3 AFTER WS-IX FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-IX > 2
           END-PERFORM
           PERFORM FILE-VERBS 2 TIMES
           GO TO FLOW-VERBS DEPENDING ON WS-RRN
           ALTER IO-ERR-PARA TO PROCEED TO FILE-VERBS
           IF WS-RRN = 1 THEN NEXT SENTENCE.
           MOVE 4 TO RETURN-CODE
           MOVE 16 TO SORT-RETURN
           ENTER COBOL.
           EXIT PROGRAM
           STOP RUN
           STOP "literal".
       STRING-VERBS.
           MOVE FUNCTION UPPER-CASE(WS-CTLAREA) TO WS-CTLAREA
           STRING WS-CTLAREA DELIMITED BY SPACE
             INTO WS-REDEF WITH POINTER WS-RRN
             ON OVERFLOW CONTINUE NOT ON OVERFLOW CONTINUE END-STRING
           UNSTRING WS-REDEF DELIMITED BY ALL "," OR ";"
             INTO WS-CTLAREA DELIMITER IN WS-STATUS
             COUNT IN WS-RRN TALLYING IN WS-RRN END-UNSTRING
           INSPECT WS-REDEF TALLYING WS-RRN FOR CHARACTERS
             BEFORE INITIAL "X" REPLACING LEADING ZEROS BY SPACES
           INSPECT WS-REDEF CONVERTING "abc" TO "ABC"
           SET WS-IX TO 1
           SET WS-IX UP BY 1
           SET WS-IX DOWN BY 1
           SET U-POINTER TO NULL
           SET U-PROCPTR TO NULLS
           MOVE HIGH-VALUES TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE HIGH-VALUE TO WS-STAT
           MOVE LOW-VALUES TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE LOW-VALUE TO WS-STAT
           MOVE QUOTES TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE QUOTE TO WS-STAT
           MOVE ZEROES TO WS-RRN
           REPLACE OFF.
       TABLE-VERBS.
           SEARCH WS-ROW VARYING WS-IX
             AT END CONTINUE
             WHEN WS-COL = "HIT" CONTINUE
           END-SEARCH
           SEARCH ALL WS-ROW
             WHEN WS-COL = "HIT" CONTINUE
           END-SEARCH.
       SORT-VERBS.
           SORT SORT-WORK ON ASCENDING KEY SORT-RECORD
             WITH DUPLICATES IN ORDER
             COLLATING SEQUENCE IS STD-1
             INPUT PROCEDURE IS FILE-VERBS
             OUTPUT PROCEDURE IS SCREEN-VERBS
           MERGE SORT-WORK ON DESCENDING KEY SORT-RECORD
             USING ORDER-FILE ARCH-FILE GIVING REL-FILE
           RELEASE SORT-RECORD FROM WS-REDEF
           RETURN SORT-WORK RECORD AT END CONTINUE END-RETURN.
       CALL-VERBS.
           CALL "NEXTPGM" USING BY REFERENCE WS-REDEF
             BY CONTENT LENGTH OF WS-REDEF BY VALUE WS-RRN
             ON EXCEPTION CONTINUE NOT ON EXCEPTION CONTINUE END-CALL
           CALL WS-CTLAREA ON OVERFLOW CONTINUE END-CALL
           CALL "NEXTPGM" RETURNING WS-RRN END-CALL
           CANCEL "NEXTPGM"
           COPY ORDCPY SUPPRESS.
       XML-VERBS.
           XML PARSE WS-OVER
             PROCESSING PROCEDURE IS IO-ERR-PARA
             ON EXCEPTION CONTINUE
             NOT ON EXCEPTION CONTINUE
           END-XML
           XML GENERATE WS-OVER FROM WS-REDEF
             COUNT IN WS-RRN END-XML
           IF XML-CODE = 0 AND XML-EVENT = "END-OF-DOCUMENT"
             MOVE XML-TEXT TO WS-CTLAREA
             MOVE XML-NTEXT TO U-NATL
           END-IF
           GOBACK.
      *
      *The intrinsic functions, each with an argument of the shape
      *its own chapter gives it.
       FUNCTION-SNIPPETS.
           MOVE FUNCTION ACOS(U-COMP-2) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION ADD-DURATION(WS-DATE DAYS 5) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION ANNUITY(U-COMP-2 12) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION ASIN(U-COMP-2) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION ATAN(U-COMP-2) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION CHAR(194) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION CONVERT-DATE-TIME
             (WS-DATE DATE) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION COS(U-COMP-2) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION CURRENT-DATE TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION DATE-OF-INTEGER(150000) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION DATE-TO-YYYYMMDD(260729) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION DAY-OF-INTEGER(150000) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION DAY-TO-YYYYDDD(26210) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION DISPLAY-OF(U-NATL) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION EXTRACT-DATE-TIME
             (WS-DATE DAYS) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION FACTORIAL(5) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION FIND-DURATION
             (WS-DATE WS-DATE DAYS) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION INTEGER(WS-AMOUNT) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION INTEGER-OF-DATE(20260729) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION INTEGER-OF-DAY(2026210) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION INTEGER-PART(WS-AMOUNT) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION LENGTH(WS-REDEF) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION LOCALE-DATE("20260729") TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION LOCALE-TIME("120000") TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION LOG(U-COMP-2) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION LOG10(U-COMP-2) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION LOWER-CASE(WS-CTLAREA) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION MAX(WS-RRN 7) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION MEAN(1 2 3) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION MEDIAN(1 2 3) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION MIDRANGE(1 2 3) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION MIN(WS-RRN 7) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION MOD(WS-RRN 7) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION NATIONAL-OF(WS-CTLAREA) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION NUMVAL(WS-CTLAREA) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION NUMVAL-C(WS-CTLAREA) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION ORD("A") TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION ORD-MAX(1 2 3) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION ORD-MIN(1 2 3) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION PARMS TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION PRESENT-VALUE(U-COMP-2 100) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION RANDOM(1) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION RANGE(1 2 3) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION REM(WS-RRN 7) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION REVERSE(WS-CTLAREA) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION SIN(U-COMP-2) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION SQRT(U-COMP-2) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION STANDARD-DEVIATION(1 2 3) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION SUBTRACT-DURATION
             (WS-DATE DAYS 5) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION SUM(1 2 3) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION TAN(U-COMP-2) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION TEST-DATE-TIME(WS-DATE DATE) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION TRIM(WS-CTLAREA) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION TRIML(WS-CTLAREA) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION TRIMR(WS-CTLAREA) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION UPPER-CASE(WS-CTLAREA) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION UTF8STRING(WS-CTLAREA) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION VARIANCE(1 2 3) TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION WHEN-COMPILED TO WS-CTLAREA
           MOVE FUNCTION YEAR-TO-YYYY(26) TO WS-CTLAREA
      *
      *The remaining reserved words, kept so the whole of
      *Appendix E stays exercised. Each is a real word of the
      *language; a snippet home for any of them is welcome.
       REMAINING-WORDS.
           ALIAS ALLOCATE ALPHABETIC ALPHANUMERIC
           ALPHANUMERIC-EDITED ATTRIBUTE AUTO BACKGROUND-COLOUR
           CLOCK-UNITS CODE CONTROLS CRT-UNDER CURSOR
           DB-FORMAT-NAME DBCS DBCS-EDITED DEBUG-CONTENTS
           DEBUG-ITEM DEBUG-LINE DEBUG-NAME DEBUG-SUB-1 DEBUG-SUB-2
           DEBUG-SUB-3 DEFAULT DESCRIBED EJECT EMPTY-CHECK
           END-DISPLAY END-INVOKE ENTRY EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
           FILE-STREAM FOREGROUND-COLOUR FREE ID INDIC INDICATE
           INDICATOR INDICATORS INITIATE INVOKE KANJI LEFT
           LEFT-JUSTIFY LENGTH-CHECK LIBRARY LOCALE METACLASS
           MODIFIED MODULES NULL-KEY-MAP NULL-MAP NUMBER
           NUMERIC-EDITED OBJECT OMITTED PADDING PREFIX PRINTING
           PROCEDURES PROCESS REFERENCES REPOSITORY RESET ROLLING
           SKIP1 SKIP2 SKIP3 SPACE-FILL STARTING SUBSTITUTE
           SYMBOLIC SYSIN SYSOUT TERMINAL TITLE VLR ZERO-FILL
      *
      *A member is a compilation group: a second program may follow
      *END PROGRAM, and a program contained inside another may be
      *COMMON, callable by its siblings.
       END PROGRAM CBLWORDS.
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. CBLTWO IS RECURSIVE PROGRAM.
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       TWO-MAIN.
           GOBACK.
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. CBLINNER IS COMMON PROGRAM.
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       INNER-MAIN.
           GOBACK.
       END PROGRAM CBLINNER.
       END PROGRAM CBLTWO.
